            <ArticleTitle>[Unstable angina in a patient with single coronary artery].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>297-302</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Single coronary artery is a rare anomaly with or without other cardiac diseases and uncertain prognostic importance. It may be related with sudden death. We report a case of 64 years old man with single coronary artery and unstable angina, successful treated with medical therapy, for long time (six years).</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
